    "faqTitle": "Frequently asked questions",
    "faq1Q": "What is Abugida?",
    "faq1A": "Abugida is an online learning platform for Ethiopian schools. Students practise with quizzes made from their own textbooks and get help from an AI tutor; teachers get classroom tools; schools get clear reports on progress.",
    "faq2Q": "Which grades and subjects does Abugida cover?",
    "faq2A": "Grades 1 to 12, aligned with the Ethiopian national curriculum — including Mathematics, Physics, Chemistry, Biology, English, Amharic, History and Geography.",
    "faq3Q": "Are the questions based on Ethiopian textbooks?",
    "faq3A": "Yes. Every practice question is written from a chapter of the textbook your grade uses, checked against the book, and comes with an explanation of the right answer.",
    "faq4Q": "How does the AI tutor help students?",
    "faq4A": "Students can ask about anything they are studying and get a clear, step-by-step answer — useful for homework, revision and exam preparation.",
    "faq5Q": "Can I use Abugida on my phone?",
    "faq5A": "Yes. Abugida works in the browser on any phone or laptop, and you can add it to your home screen like an app. Android and iOS apps are on the way.",
    "faq6Q": "How can a school or teacher join?",
    "faq6A": "Schools sign up with Abugida, and the school admin then adds its teachers and enrols students by grade and section. School students sign in with a username from their school — no email needed.",
    "faq7Q": "Is Abugida available in Amharic?",
    "faq7A": "Yes. You can switch the app between English and Amharic at any time.",
